---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How it works"
  description="Anchor uses spaced retrieval in the family WhatsApp chat so Athina can practise remembering — gently, on her own schedule."
  currentPath="/how-it-works"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>How it works</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Anchor lives in the group chat the family already uses. No new app. No training sessions. Just memories coming back at the right time.
    </p>

    <h2>Family shares a moment</h2>
    <p>
      Sofia or Maria drops a photo, a voice note, or a short line into WhatsApp — Maria's first day of school, Sunday lunch, a walk by the sea.
      Anchor saves it as a practiceable memory.
    </p>

    <h2>Spaced retrieval</h2>
    <p>
      Later, Anchor asks Athina a gentle question that brings the moment back without giving the answer away.
      Remembering freely stretches the wait. A cue holds the schedule. A struggle resets to tomorrow.
    </p>

    <h2>She stays in the story</h2>
    <p>
      The family keeps talking. Athina keeps her place in it — not as a patient of a new tool, but as grandmother in the same chat.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top: 2rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/app">Try the interactive demo</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
